diff --git a/.changes/runtime-custom-protocol-http.md b/.changes/runtime-custom-protocol-http.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4cc22b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changes/runtime-custom-protocol-http.md
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+---
+'tauri-runtime': 'minor:enhance'
+'tauri': 'minor:enhance'
+---
+
+Add the defaulted `Runtime::CUSTOM_PROTOCOLS_USE_HTTP` opt-in for custom runtimes to use HTTP(S) custom-protocol URLs on any platform. App URLs, asset URL conversion, local IPC classification, and isolation/proxy URLs honor the runtime convention. Native runtime defaults are unchanged. Local bundled and HTTP-mapped protocol authorities now reject nondefault ports and credentials. The runtime remains responsible for in-process loading and browser security policy enforcement; this does not change the initial-webview-origin policy of asset CORS response headers.
